# AGENTS.md

## Required Start

Start from the small bootstrap, then load only the context the actual operation
needs. Do not read the same documentation twice by pre-loading architecture,
workflow, and quality documents before requesting context.

{% if governance == "managed" %}
Tier 0 bootstrap identifies repository rules, governance mode, the active task,
and how to request more context:

```bash
make agent-status
```

Tier 1 task/skill context is loaded deterministically for the actual work:

```bash
make agent-context TASK=<id>
make agent-context TASK=<id> SKILL=<skill>
make agent-context TASK=<id> SKILL=<skill> MODE=resume
```

Respect exactly one active managed task and use the generated context bundle.
Use the default context mode for a new task; use `MODE=resume` when resuming or
fixing an existing PR.
{% else %}
This project uses lightweight governance. There is no mandatory task state
machine for ordinary implementation work. Tier 0 bootstrap is `AGENTS.md` and
`project/brief.md`. Tier 1 context is the files directly relevant to the
operation and any selected skill's declared reads. Tier 2 exploration opens
specific files under `docs/`, `project/`, and the source tree on demand; never
recursively load a directory into context.
{% endif %}

## Architecture Rules

- Start from the current project type: `{{ project_type }}`.
- Start from the current runtime level: `{{ runtime_level }}`.
- Start from the current governance mode: `{{ governance }}`.
- Use the simplest architecture that satisfies the current requirement.
- Keep business rules independently testable from transport concerns.
- Introduce abstractions only when repetition, coupling, complexity, or an explicit requirement justifies them.
- Do not add databases, queues, caches, external services, authentication, Kubernetes, or production deployment unless a concrete requirement and ADR justify it.
{% if project_type in ["backend", "fullstack"] %}
- Backend business rules belong outside FastAPI route handlers.
{% endif %}
{% if project_type in ["frontend", "fullstack"] %}
- Frontend pages compose features; feature logic belongs in feature composables or services when the feature has meaningful behavior.
{% endif %}
{% if project_type == "fullstack" %}
- API types must be generated from OpenAPI once a backend API contract exists.
{% endif %}

